      ],
      "explanation": "\\((-2x^2y)\\cdot(3xy^2)=-6x^3y^3\\). Substituting gives \\(-6\\times1\\times(-1)=6\\).",
      "id": "multiply-then-substitute",
      "sourceRef": "cn-math/cnm_144_q3#multiply-then-substitute",
      "title": "Multiply, then substitute"
    },
    {
      "directNodeIds": [
        "cnm_029"
      ],
      "explanation": "Since the variable values are given, evaluate each factor directly. Substituting \\(x=1\\) and \\(y=-1\\) gives\n\\[\n-2x^2y=-2\\cdot1^2\\cdot(-1)=2,\n\\]\n\\[\n3xy^2=3\\cdot1\\cdot(-1)^2=3.\n\\]\nTheir product is \\(2\\cdot3=6\\).",
      "id": "substitute-each-factor",
      "sourceRef": "cn-math/cnm_144_q3#substitute-each-factor",
      "title": "Evaluate each factor directly"
